            <title>[LU-21193] sanity-ec test_35c: domain N objects min X max Y, uneven RR balance across OSTs in a failure domain</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21193</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;sanity-ec test_35c ("check RR balance with unequal failure domains", added by &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19823" title="FLR-EC: Integrate failure domains with stripe allocator for EC" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-19823"&gt;LU-19823&lt;/a&gt; commit 19e1c99246) fails intermittently with "domain N objects min X max Y": OSTs in the same failure domain receive uneven numbers of EC objects, and the check requires max*4 &amp;lt;= min*5.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Examples (domain 2 is the one with two OSTs in these runs; domain 1 and 3 balanced at 40 and 80 objects):&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class="alternate" type="square"&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;lustre-reviews 66678 ps8, review-dne-zfs-part-7, session 1a5f1362-c3fc-4145-9599-6c5848647721: domain 2 objects min 42 max 118 (OST4 118, OST6 42)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;lustre-master-next full-part-3, session 27d55436-8049-4762-b287-1855987dce21: domain 2 objects min 41 max 99&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;lustre-master-next full-part-3, session dcfb2c6c-5a31-403d-897b-a3546c5e5755: domain 2 objects min 10 max 130&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;an earlier variant: domain 2 objects min 1 max 139&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Rate: about 1.8% of lustre-reviews review-dne-zfs-part-7 runs (4 of 221 in 30 days), 3 failures in about 145 full-part-3 runs on master and master-next; no failures in the ldiskfs review-dne-part-7 runs (0 of 218). The failing change (66678, MGS sptlrpc llogs) does not touch LOD or sanity-ec. The unequal-domain RR allocation from &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19823" title="FLR-EC: Integrate failure domains with stripe allocator for EC" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-19823"&gt;LU-19823&lt;/a&gt; / &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21014" title="FLR-EC: Fix overstriping bug in EC allocations" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-21014"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-21014&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; / &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-8933" title="sanity test_51d: object distribution between OSTs not even" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-8933"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-8933&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; area appears to leave one OST of a domain short, so either the allocator or the test's 25% tolerance needs work. No ticket covered this signature before.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Raised by Patch Watcher run pw-engineer-66678-ps8-c587e80f6f1e on &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/66678" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/66678&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
